{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "hdbscan-title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# HDBSCAN — Clustering sur l'échantillon annoté (420 profils)\n",
    "\n",
    "Ce notebook applique **HDBSCAN** (Hierarchical Density-Based Spatial Clustering of Applications with Noise) sur les 420 profils labellisés.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pourquoi HDBSCAN ?**\n",
    "- Ne nécessite pas de fixer K à l'avance\n",
    "- Identifie les profils atypiques comme **bruit** (`label = -1`)\n",
    "- Gère des densités variables (contrairement à DBSCAN)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objectif** : comparer la structure trouvée par HDBSCAN avec les labels humains/bots et avec les autres approches non-supervisées (K-means, Spectral)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "imports",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "import-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import polars as pl\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score, normalized_mutual_info_score, silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# HDBSCAN — installer si nécessaire : pip install hdbscan\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import hdbscan\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    raise ImportError(\"hdbscan n'est pas installé. Lancez : pip install hdbscan\")\n",
    "\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(Path.cwd().parents[2]))\n",
    "from src.ml.features import get_labeled_features\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 120\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Imports OK\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "load-data",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Chargement et prétraitement"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "load-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# Mêmes features que le notebook Random Forest\n",
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "ALL_FEATURES = [\n",
    "    \"verified\", \"default_profile\", \"default_profile_image\",\n",
    "    \"tweet_count\", \"urls_per_tweet\", \"hashtags_per_tweet\", \"mentions_per_tweet\",\n",
    "    \"retweet_rate\", \"reply_rate\", \"unique_sources\", \"bot_source_ratio\",\n",
    "    \"followers_friends_ratio\", \"reputation\", \"favourites_per_status\",\n",
    "    \"listed_per_follower\", \"account_age_days\", \"days_since_last_tweet\",\n",
    "    \"observation_span_days\", \"tweet_frequency\", \"tweets_per_day_in_dataset\",\n",
    "    \"description_length\", \"has_description\", \"has_url\", \"has_location\",\n",
    "    \"screen_name_length\", \"screen_name_has_digits\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "LOG_FEATURES = [\n",
    "    \"tweet_count\", \"account_age_days\", \"days_since_last_tweet\",\n",
    "    \"observation_span_days\", \"description_length\", \"screen_name_length\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df = get_labeled_features(\"data/processed/labeling_sample.csv\")\n",
    "df_model = df.select(ALL_FEATURES + [\"label\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Conversion en float + log-transform\n",
    "X = df_model.select(ALL_FEATURES).to_pandas().astype(float)\n",
    "for col in LOG_FEATURES:\n",
    "    X[col] = np.log1p(np.maximum(X[col], 0))\n",
    "\n",
    "y = df_model[\"label\"].to_pandas()\n",
    "\n",
    "# StandardScaler\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"X shape: {X_scaled.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Labels: {y.value_counts().sort_index().to_dict()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "hdbscan-fit",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. HDBSCAN\n",
    "\n",
    "Paramètres clés :\n",
    "- `min_samples` : nombre minimum de points dans le voisinage pour qu'un point soit considéré comme "core"\n",
    "- `min_cluster_size` : taille minimum d'un cluster valide\n",
    "\n",
    "On teste plusieurs combinaisons."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "hdbscan-grid",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "configs = [\n",
    "    {\"min_samples\": 3, \"min_cluster_size\": 10},\n",
    "    {\"min_samples\": 5, \"min_cluster_size\": 15},\n",
    "    {\"min_samples\": 5, \"min_cluster_size\": 20},\n",
    "    {\"min_samples\": 10, \"min_cluster_size\": 20},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "for cfg in configs:\n",
    "    clusterer = hdbscan.HDBSCAN(\n",
    "        min_samples=cfg[\"min_samples\"],\n",
    "        min_cluster_size=cfg[\"min_cluster_size\"],\n",
    "        metric=\"euclidean\",\n",
    "        cluster_selection_method=\"eom\",  # Excess of Mass\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    labels_hdb = clusterer.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    n_clusters = len(set(labels_hdb)) - (1 if -1 in labels_hdb else 0)\n",
    "    n_noise = list(labels_hdb).count(-1)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    ari = adjusted_rand_score(y, labels_hdb) if len(set(labels_hdb)) > 1 else 0\n",
    "    nmi = normalized_mutual_info_score(y, labels_hdb) if len(set(labels_hdb)) > 1 else 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    results.append({\n",
    "        \"min_samples\": cfg[\"min_samples\"],\n",
    "        \"min_cluster_size\": cfg[\"min_cluster_size\"],\n",
    "        \"n_clusters\": n_clusters,\n",
    "        \"n_noise\": n_noise,\n",
    "        \"ARI\": ari,\n",
    "        \"NMI\": nmi,\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "results_df = pl.DataFrame(results)\n",
    "print(results_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sélection de la meilleure config selon ARI\n",
    "best_idx = results_df[\"ARI\"].arg_max()\n",
    "best_cfg = configs[best_idx]\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✅ Meilleure config : {best_cfg}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "hdbscan-best",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Ré-entraînement avec la meilleure config\n",
    "clusterer = hdbscan.HDBSCAN(\n",
    "    min_samples=best_cfg[\"min_samples\"],\n",
    "    min_cluster_size=best_cfg[\"min_cluster_size\"],\n",
    "    metric=\"euclidean\",\n",
    "    cluster_selection_method=\"eom\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "labels_hdb = clusterer.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Clusters trouvés : {sorted(set(labels_hdb))}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Bruit (-1) : {(labels_hdb == -1).sum()} / {len(labels_hdb)} ({(labels_hdb == -1).mean()*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Distribution des vrais labels par cluster HDBSCAN\n",
    "cross_tab = pl.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"hdbscan_label\": labels_hdb,\n",
    "    \"true_label\": y,\n",
    "}).group_by([\"hdbscan_label\", \"true_label\"]).len().sort([\"hdbscan_label\", \"true_label\"])\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Tableau croisé HDBSCAN vs Labels ===\")\n",
    "print(cross_tab)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "visualisation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Visualisation (PCA 2D)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "viz-pca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pca = PCA(n_components=2)\n",
    "X_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1 : vrais labels\n",
    "colors_true = [\"#4caf50\" if l == 0 else \"#f44336\" for l in y]\n",
    "axes[0].scatter(X_pca[:, 0], X_pca[:, 1], c=colors_true, alpha=0.7, s=40, edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Vrais labels (Vert=Humain, Rouge=Bot)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(f\"PC1 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[0]*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(f\"PC2 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[1]*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 2 : HDBSCAN clusters\n",
    "unique_labels = sorted(set(labels_hdb))\n",
    "cmap = plt.cm.get_cmap(\"tab10\", len(unique_labels))\n",
    "for label in unique_labels:\n",
    "    mask = labels_hdb == label\n",
    "    color = \"gray\" if label == -1 else cmap(label)\n",
    "    label_name = f\"Bruit (-1)\" if label == -1 else f\"Cluster {label}\"\n",
    "    axes[1].scatter(\n",
    "        X_pca[mask, 0], X_pca[mask, 1],\n",
    "        c=[color], alpha=0.7, s=40,\n",
    "        edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.5,\n",
    "        label=label_name,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"HDBSCAN clusters\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(f\"PC1 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[0]*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(f\"PC2 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[1]*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Comparaison : Labels réels vs HDBSCAN (PCA 2D)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "analyse-bruit",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Analyse du bruit HDBSCAN (`label = -1`)\n",
    "\n",
    "Le cluster `-1` (bruit) représente les profils que HDBSCAN considère comme ne rentrant dans aucun groupe dense. Ce sont nos **candidats atypiques**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "noise-analysis",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "noise_mask = labels_hdb == -1\n",
    "noise_indices = np.where(noise_mask)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Profils classés 'bruit' : {len(noise_indices)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Dont bots (label=1) : {y[noise_mask].sum()} ({y[noise_mask].mean()*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Dont humains (label=0) : {(~y[noise_mask].astype(bool)).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Comparaison : les bots sont-ils sur-représentés dans le bruit ?\n",
    "bot_rate_noise = y[noise_mask].mean()\n",
    "bot_rate_global = y.mean()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTaux de bots dans le bruit : {bot_rate_noise*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Taux de bots global : {bot_rate_global*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Sur-représentation : {bot_rate_noise / bot_rate_global:.2f}x\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Top features des profils "bruit"\n",
    "noise_profiles = X.iloc[noise_indices]\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Moyennes des features (bruit vs global) ===\")\n",
    "comparison = pl.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"feature\": X.columns,\n",
    "    \"bruit_mean\": noise_profiles.mean().values,\n",
    "    \"global_mean\": X.mean().values,\n",
    "}).with_columns(\n",
    "    (pl.col(\"bruit_mean\") / pl.col(\"global_mean\")).alias(\"ratio\")\n",
    ").sort(\"ratio\", descending=True)\n",
    "print(comparison.head(15))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "soft-clustering",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Soft clustering : probabilités d'appartenance\n",
    "\n",
    "HDBSCAN fournit des probabilités de cluster membership. Les profils avec une probabilité faible sont "incertains" — potentiellement atypiques."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "soft-proba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "probas = clusterer.probabilities_\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "ax.hist(probas, bins=30, color=\"steelblue\", edgecolor=\"white\", alpha=0.8)\n",
    "ax.axvline(probas.mean(), color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"Moyenne = {probas.mean():.2f}\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Probabilité d'appartenance au cluster\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Nombre de profils\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Distribution des probabilités HDBSCAN\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Profils avec probabilité < 0.5 (incertains)\n",
    "uncertain = probas < 0.5\n",
    "print(f\"Profils incertains (proba < 0.5) : {uncertain.sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Dont bots : {y[uncertain].sum()} ({y[uncertain].mean()*100:.1f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "synthese",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Synthèse\n",
    "\n",
    "| Métrique | Valeur | Interprétation |\n",
    "|----------|--------|----------------|\n",
    "| ARI (vs labels) | *à remplir* | Concordance avec la ground truth |\n",
    "| NMI (vs labels) | *à remplir* | Information mutuelle |\n",
    "| % bruit | *à remplir* | Profils considérés atypiques |\n",
    "| % bots dans le bruit | *à remplir* | Capacité de détection |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Points clés à discuter dans le rapport :**\n",
    "- Les bots sont-ils sur-représentés dans le bruit HDBSCAN ?\n",
    "- Les clusters trouvés correspondent-ils à des populations sémantiques (humains vs bots) ?\n",
    "- Comparaison avec K-means et Spectral (via ARI croisé dans le notebook `comparison_420.ipynb`)."
   ]
  }
 ],
